3  Visual Binaries:  Masses and the Relative Orbit
From a well-observed visual binary we can determine:  (1) parallax, (2) proper motion, (3) eccentricity,
(4) angular size of the orbit, (5) total mass, (6) inclination of the orbit.  For a face-on system the
radial velocity is zero.
