Classification of planets:(1) rocky planets; (2) giant planets, which split into (i)hot Jupiters—
Jupiter-sized planets orbiting very close to their star — and (ii) ice giants.
Transmission spectroscopy.If starlight passes through the atmosphere of a hot Jupiter during
transit, extra absorption lines from the planet’s atmosphere appear in the star’s spectrum.
Useful terms.Epoch:  the reference time from which phase is counted.Photometric variability:
brightness changes with time, recorded as a light curve.
