Figure 18:Variants of the eclipse light curve.
Limb darkening.A stellar disc is brighter at its centre than at its edge.  As the eclipsing body
moves from the dim limb towards the bright centre it blocks more and more light, so the bottom of
the light curve is curved instead of flat.
